<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no sales -USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no sales -USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry and demand light. Sales confirmed this week on 81,700 head including 20,100 head or about 25 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>Last sales Thursday, April 24 at 67.00, bids Friday morning 66.00-67.00, asking prices 67.00-69.00. Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
